  outer list: updated every 100 steps, buffer 0.272 nm, rlist 1.472 nm
  inner list: updated every  20 steps, buffer 0.083 nm, rlist 1.283 nm

The non-bonded pair calculation algorithm tolerates a few missing pair interactions close to the cut-off. This can lead to a systematic overestimation of the pressure due to missing LJ interactions. The error in the average pressure due to missing LJ interactions is at most 2.09 bar.
The pressure error can be controlled by setting the environment variable GMX_VERLET_BUFFER_PRESSURE_TOLERANCE to the allowed error in units of bar.

